WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.576 --> 00:00:17.144
Dick and Hobbs had written to Cedric about their ideas to help him.

2
00:00:18.685 --> 00:00:21.006
After that, they didn't know what else to do.

3
00:00:22.087 --> 00:00:23.828
But they had plenty to discuss.

4
00:00:26.409 --> 00:00:31.432
Every day the New York newspapers ran fresh stories about Cedric and the new Lord Fauntleroy.

5
00:00:32.732 --> 00:00:33.532
Every night Mr.

6
00:00:33.552 --> 00:00:36.033
Hobbs read the latest stories aloud to Dick.

7
00:00:36.053 --> 00:00:41.034
"It seems like this Earl of Dorincourt is an important guy," Dick said.

8
00:00:41.054 --> 00:00:46.316
"He's got tons of money, and his castle sounds like a grand place.

9
00:00:47.596 --> 00:00:50.737
Imagine our Cedric living in a fancy, old castle!"

10
00:00:50.757 --> 00:00:54.898
"Unfortunately, he may not be living there much longer."

11
00:00:55.839 --> 00:00:57.859
Mr. Hobbs put down the newspaper.

12
00:00:57.879 --> 00:01:00.220
"He's such a good kid.

13
00:01:01.408 --> 00:01:03.429
What's happened to him is a real shame."

14
00:01:06.390 --> 00:01:09.752
The next morning Dick was shining the boots of a regular customer.

15
00:01:10.832 --> 00:01:14.293
Mr. Bennington was a young man, just starting out as a lawyer.

16
00:01:15.394 --> 00:01:17.235
He always enjoyed talking to Dick.

17
00:01:18.975 --> 00:01:19.876
That day Mr.

18
00:01:19.916 --> 00:01:22.777
Bennington was reading a newspaper while Dick worked.

19
00:01:22.797 --> 00:01:25.798
"Have you heard about this earl in England?

20
00:01:26.619 --> 00:01:29.780
Turns out there are two kids, both claiming to be his heir.

21
00:01:30.840 --> 00:01:32.921
The Earl of Dorincourt—" "What?"

22
00:01:33.782 --> 00:01:36.204
Dick looked up from the man's boots in surprise.

23
00:01:37.565 --> 00:01:40.627
Mr. Bennington turned the paper so Dick could see a photo.

24
00:01:40.647 --> 00:01:43.409
"This is the new Lord Fauntleroy's mother.

25
00:01:44.449 --> 00:01:45.390
She's a handsome woman."

26
00:01:46.491 --> 00:01:49.032
Mr. Bennington noticed Dick's expression.

27
00:01:49.052 --> 00:01:51.154
"What's the matter with you?"

28
00:01:53.115 --> 00:01:56.057
Dick was staring wide-eyed and open-mouthed.

29
00:01:57.198 --> 00:02:00.020
He pointed to the woman, who had thick, dark hair.

30
00:02:01.616 --> 00:02:02.276
"I know her!"

31
00:02:02.576 --> 00:02:03.197
Dick said.

32
00:02:07.098 --> 00:02:07.418
you do."

33
00:02:08.078 --> 00:02:09.478
Mr. Bennington laughed.

34
00:02:09.498 --> 00:02:12.699
"And I'm best friends with the queen!"

35
00:02:13.760 --> 00:02:16.640
He shrugged as Dick continued to stare.

36
00:02:16.660 --> 00:02:20.001
"I'm finished with the paper if you want it."

37
00:02:20.882 --> 00:02:21.602
"I do want it!"

38
00:02:22.502 --> 00:02:25.203
Dick hurriedly put away his cloths and polishes.

39
00:02:25.223 --> 00:02:28.264
"And I'm closing down the stand for the day!"

40
00:02:29.524 --> 00:02:32.486
Mr. Bennington counted out the coins for his shoeshine.

41
00:02:32.506 --> 00:02:37.270
"I have no idea what's bothering you, but it sounds serious."

42
00:02:39.291 --> 00:02:42.673
A few minutes later, Dick was racing through the streets toward Mr.

43
00:02:42.714 --> 00:02:43.554
Hobbs' store.

44
00:02:45.135 --> 00:02:47.937
Dick was so out of breath that he could hardly speak.

45
00:02:47.957 --> 00:02:54.822
"Look at this He handed the newspaper to Mr.

46
00:02:54.862 --> 00:02:57.364
Hobbs. "What am I looking at?"

47
00:02:57.780 --> 00:02:59.721
Mr. Hobbs put down his broom.

48
00:02:59.741 --> 00:03:02.483
"The woman in this picture!"

49
00:03:02.803 --> 00:03:03.563
Dick shouted.

50
00:03:03.583 --> 00:03:05.724
"She's no lord's wife!

51
00:03:06.705 --> 00:03:08.486
That's Minna—my brother's wife!

52
00:03:09.706 --> 00:03:11.888
I'd know her anywhere, and so would Ben."

53
00:03:13.328 --> 00:03:16.850
Mr. Hobbs dropped into his chair and studied the newspaper.

54
00:03:16.870 --> 00:03:19.452
"I was right!

55
00:03:20.532 --> 00:03:23.494
Those aristocrats have cheated Cedric out of his title!"

56
00:03:23.514 --> 00:03:27.536
"No, Minna is the one who's cheated Cedric."

57
00:03:28.704 --> 00:03:30.545
Dick stamped his foot in anger.

58
00:03:30.565 --> 00:03:34.929
"As soon as I saw her picture, I remembered another story we'd read.

59
00:03:36.150 --> 00:03:39.312
It mentioned that the new Lord Fauntleroy has a scar on his chin."

60
00:03:39.332 --> 00:03:42.994
"Just like your nephew!"

61
00:03:43.014 --> 00:03:46.277
Mr. Hobbs was now as angry as Dick.

62
00:03:46.297 --> 00:03:48.518
"That's right!

63
00:03:49.699 --> 00:03:51.761
Tom got that scar when Minna threw the plate.

64
00:03:52.842 --> 00:03:55.924
He's no more Lord Fauntleroy than I am," Dick said.

65
00:03:57.152 --> 00:03:59.093
"We have to do something right now!"

66
00:04:00.273 --> 00:04:05.996
Mr. Hobbs sank into his chair, overwhelmed by the problem, but Dick was full of energy.

67
00:04:06.016 --> 00:04:10.137
"Hand me some scissors, so I can cut out this picture," Dick said.

68
00:04:10.157 --> 00:04:13.179
"I'm going to send it to Ben."

69
00:04:13.199 --> 00:04:17.840
"I'll write to Cedric—and the earl."

70
00:04:19.701 --> 00:04:23.203
They were in the midst of their letters when Dick had another idea.

71
00:04:23.223 --> 00:04:26.444
"That guy who gave me the newspaper is a lawyer.

72
00:04:27.512 --> 00:04:28.513
Maybe he can help us."

73
00:04:30.013 --> 00:04:33.314
Mr. Hobbs was immediately impressed by Dick's suggestion.

74
00:04:33.334 --> 00:04:35.675
"You're absolutely right.

75
00:04:36.796 --> 00:04:38.597
This situation calls for a lawyer."

76
00:04:40.337 --> 00:04:42.978
Mr. Bennington was surprised when Dick and Mr.

77
00:04:42.998 --> 00:04:44.539
Hobbs arrived at his office.

78
00:04:44.559 --> 00:04:48.841
"You've already shined my boots once today," Mr.

79
00:04:48.881 --> 00:04:50.461
Bennington said with a smile.

80
00:04:50.481 --> 00:04:53.242
"Are you looking for more customers?"

81
00:04:54.603 --> 00:04:55.523
"This is my friend Mr.

82
00:04:55.563 --> 00:04:57.637
Hobbs, and we need your help," Dick said.

83
00:04:57.657 --> 00:05:00.098
"It's about that newspaper story."

84
00:05:01.379 --> 00:05:04.722
He quickly described how Cedric had become Lord Fauntleroy.

85
00:05:06.063 --> 00:05:10.306
Mr. Bennington took notes as Dick talked about Minna and her son, Tom.

86
00:05:10.326 --> 00:05:13.729
"I've read about this woman before.

87
00:05:14.950 --> 00:05:17.051
Parts of her story don't make sense."

88
00:05:18.072 --> 00:05:20.554
Mr. Bennington tapped his pen on his desk.

89
00:05:20.574 --> 00:05:23.296
"There's no harm in investigating this.

90
00:05:24.296 --> 00:05:27.598
I'm not busy right now, and the publicity may give my career a boost."

91
00:05:28.898 --> 00:05:30.979
"I don't care what you charge," Mr.

92
00:05:30.999 --> 00:05:31.679
Hobbs said.

93
00:05:31.699 --> 00:05:34.901
"Send me the bill, and I'll gladly pay it."

94
00:05:34.921 --> 00:05:41.724
"My first task is to write to Dick's brother, Ben, and to the earl's lawyer."

95
00:05:42.604 --> 00:05:44.665
Mr. Bennington pulled out some paper.

96
00:05:46.566 --> 00:05:48.067
When the two friends left Mr.

97
00:05:48.087 --> 00:05:50.228
Bennington's office, they were full of hope.

98
00:05:51.804 --> 00:05:53.085
At midnight Dick and Mr.

99
00:05:53.105 --> 00:05:55.247
Hobbs were still talking in the grocery store.

100
00:05:58.769 --> 00:05:59.270
One of Mr.

101
00:05:59.290 --> 00:06:02.112
Bennington's letters was on a train speeding westward.

102
00:06:04.254 --> 00:06:06.936
The other was on a ship sailing eastward for England.
